§ `Agent-facing offence screen`

-- Combines the encoded offence tests. A TRUE on a limb is an indication that
-- the facts as asserted would constitute that offence, subject to s 6 (general
-- exceptions already applied in the wrappers). It is not a conviction.

§§ `The Schedule to section 4B, as far as this encoding screens it`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, the Schedule to s 4B"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a specified offence in the Schedule` IF
        `the proposed act constitutes theft` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes dishonest misappropriation` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes criminal breach of trust` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes cheating` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes section 424A fraud` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes section 424B fraud` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes forgery` a
    -- items 3 to 9 and 11 of the Schedule, as far as their sections are encoded
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes aggravated theft` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes extortion` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes robbery` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes gang-robbery` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a gang-robbery preparatory offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes misappropriation of a deceased person property` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes aggravated criminal breach of trust` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a stolen property offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a fraudulent disposition` a
    -- items 1 and 2: communicating false information of a harmful thing and placing or sending a thing causing fear of harm, ss 268A to 268C
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a hoax of a harmful thing` a
    -- items 13 and 14: forgery and related offences under ss 465 to 477A, currency under ss 489A to 489I
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes aggravated forgery` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a forged document offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a false instrument equipment offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes fraudulent cancellation of a will or valuable security` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes falsification of accounts` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes a counterfeit currency offence` a
    OR  `the proposed act constitutes an altered currency offence` a

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4B"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified offence is deemed committed in Singapore` IF
        `the conduct is a specified offence in the Schedule` a
    AND `section 4B location facts are met` a

§§ `Section 4A on the encoded Chapter 6 and 6B tests`

-- chapter-1-preliminary.l4 decides s 4A on the caller's assertion that the act would
-- be a Chapter 6 or Chapter 6B offence if committed in Singapore. Both Chapters are
-- now encoded, so the same conclusion is reached here from the tests themselves;
-- the caller-asserted route is kept, and the two are disjoined in the reach rule.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 4A"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A on the encoded tests` IF
        (a's `actor`)'s `is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND a's `place of the act` EQUALS `wholly outside Singapore`
    AND (   `a Chapter 6 offence is made out` (a's `state offence`)
         OR `constitutes genocide` (a's `genocide`))

§§ `Singapore reach for the proposed act`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 2, 3, 4, 4A, 4B"
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` IF
        `the act is committed within Singapore` a
    OR  `the act is dealt with under this Code as if committed within Singapore` a
    OR  `the act is deemed committed in Singapore by a public servant` a
    OR  `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A` a
    OR  `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A on the encoded tests` a
    OR  `the specified offence is deemed committed in Singapore` a

