§§ `Build the screen`

@ref "Penal Code 1871"
@export Screen a proposed act against the encoded Penal Code 1871 offence tests for AI-agent compliance
GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act` @desc One bundle of facts about the actor and the proposed act. Nested records: actor (age, citizenship, public servant), place of the act, fault (dishonestly / fraudulently), deception (cheating), personal information dealing, services obtained, fraud conduct, property taking, trust, document making, forged document, currency, speech, abetment, conspiracy, attempt, the Chapter 16 and 17 groups, and the Chapter 6 to 15 groups (state offence, piracy, genocide, armed forces offence, unlawful assembly, public servant offence, contempt of authority, false evidence, public justice, government stamp, public nuisance, public health and safety, obscenity, racial offence). Set only the flags that are true of the proposed act; leave the rest false.
GIVETH AN `Offence Screen`
DECIDE `the offence screen of` a IS
    `Offence Screen` WITH
        `Singapore has territorial reach` IS `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` a
        , `a general exception applies` IS `a general exception applies` a
        , `a private defence justification applies s 96` IS `a private defence justification applies` a
        , `another written law may still apply s 5` IS `another written law is unaffected and may still apply` a
        , `a mistake of law is a defence s 79A` IS `a mistake of law or ignorance of the law is a defence to the charge` (a's `exception facts`)
        , `cheating s 415` IS `the proposed act constitutes cheating` a
        , `cheating by personation s 416` IS `the proposed act constitutes cheating by personation` a
        , `cheating by remote communication s 416B` IS `the proposed act constitutes cheating by remote communication` a
        , `illegally obtained personal information s 416A` IS `the proposed act constitutes illegally obtained personal information offence` a
        , `cheating and dishonestly inducing delivery of property s 420` IS `the proposed act constitutes section 420 cheating` a
        , `obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently s 420A` IS `the proposed act constitutes obtaining services dishonestly or fraudulently` a
        , `theft s 378` IS `the proposed act constitutes theft` a
        , `dishonest misappropriation s 403` IS `the proposed act constitutes dishonest misappropriation` a
        , `criminal breach of trust s 405` IS `the proposed act constitutes criminal breach of trust` a
        , `fraud s 424A` IS `the proposed act constitutes section 424A fraud` a
        , `fraud s 424B` IS `the proposed act constitutes section 424B fraud` a
        , `forgery s 463` IS `the proposed act constitutes forgery` a
        , `defamation s 499` IS `the proposed act constitutes defamation` a
        , `criminal intimidation s 503` IS `the proposed act constitutes criminal intimidation` a
        , `intentional insult s 504` IS `the proposed act constitutes intentional insult to provoke a breach of the peace` a
        , `statements conducing to public mischief s 505` IS `the proposed act constitutes statements conducing to public mischief` a
        , `abetment ss 107 and 108` IS `the proposed act constitutes abetment of an offence` a
        , `criminal conspiracy s 120A` IS `the proposed act constitutes a criminal conspiracy` a
        , `attempt s 511` IS `the proposed act constitutes an attempt` a
